      "content": "The \"mules\" concept is risky if they are ever detained for questioning. We need something more sophisticated than physical agents. \n\nIf we are to use \"standardized coding\" as you suggested in point 4, I need a way to embed our most sensitive directives within the regular, mundane daily briefing documents. These documents are read by dozens of staff members every morning. How can we design a steganographic system—perhaps through subtle linguistic cues or specific metadata patterns—that allows the Chancellor to recognize a high-priority directive hidden within a routine report, without the administrative staff ever realizing they are looking at a coded message?",
